WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.641
- You look so great.

00:00:01.641 --> 00:00:02.474
- Thank you.

00:00:02.474 --> 00:00:03.479
- I love your whole outfit.

00:00:03.479 --> 00:00:05.334
- Oh, thank you.
- Yeah, have a seat.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.167
Get comfortable.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:07.458
- It's kinda tone on tone, you know?

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:08.499
- Yeah, you blend in, yeah.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:08.499 --> 00:00:09.707
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:09.707 --> 00:00:11.165
This is great backstage.

00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:12.123
This is my first time here.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:12.956
- It is! It is your first here--

00:00:12.956 --> 00:00:13.953
- Nice dressing room.

00:00:13.953 --> 00:00:15.548
Great host everyone.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.214
- Oh, thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:18.586
We lucked out with a dressing room.

00:00:18.586 --> 00:00:19.419
- Huh?

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.252
- We lucked out with the dressing rooms.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.549
- Oh my God.
- They're huge.

00:00:21.549 --> 00:00:23.242
- Huge, they're usually
jammed in these little rooms.

00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:24.794
- You're in a closet with
like three other people--

00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:26.120
- Hundred percent.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:26.953
- Doing hair, makeup, wardrobe.

00:00:26.953 --> 00:00:27.786
- Yeah, now that's great.

00:00:27.786 --> 00:00:29.907
- We lucked out, but I heard
there's a congratulations

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:31.339
in order, you recently got engaged?

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:32.172
- I did.
(audience applaud)

00:00:32.172 --> 00:00:33.005
- That's exciting.

00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:34.820
(Eric laughing)

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:35.653
That's so exciting.

00:00:35.653 --> 00:00:37.760
How did you propose if
you don't mind me asking?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.950
- Well, everyone knows, that
follows me on social media

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.077
that I mess around with
my girlfriend a lot

00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:44.114
and prank her a lot.

00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:48.411
So I knew I had to be
really clever and creative

00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:50.575
so she wouldn't be onto to me.

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:54.212
So I pretended like there was
a company that was interested

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:56.256
in us doing a social
media campaign together.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.089
(Kelly chuckles)

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.675
And I said, we need to send
in like a chemistry video.

00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:00.508
- This is like a deep lie--

00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:02.174
- So do your hair, do your makeup.

00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:04.247
So she would be beautiful in the moment.

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:05.642
And she wanted to be beautiful.

00:01:05.642 --> 00:01:07.241
And so I set up the camera,
had a couple other cameras

00:01:07.241 --> 00:01:09.864
and then pretended that we
were gonna ask her a question

00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:12.415
but the question was
actually, "Will you marry me?"

00:01:12.415 --> 00:01:13.926
- That's so great, I love that.

00:01:13.926 --> 00:01:16.720
- Yeah, and it's documented
right there in her...

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.259
It's all captured right there.

00:01:18.259 --> 00:01:20.342
- That's so sweet and thoughtful.

00:01:20.342 --> 00:01:21.175
Like I love that.

00:01:21.175 --> 00:01:22.153
- I can't decide where to put myself--

00:01:22.153 --> 00:01:22.986
- You know what?

00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:24.730
I'm so short, I have no legs--
- That hurt.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.313
Like I'm all torso.

00:01:27.278 --> 00:01:29.231
So I've just sit so far up in my seat.

00:01:29.231 --> 00:01:31.430
Cause otherwise I'm like Lily
Tomlin in that big chair.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:32.263
(Eric chuckles)

00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:33.096
- I know.

00:01:33.096 --> 00:01:34.650
- My seat don't touch the ground.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.267
But if you wanna put pillows
behind you, that's what I do.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:38.205
- Maybe I'll hug it like this.

00:01:38.205 --> 00:01:40.194
- Just hug one.

00:01:40.194 --> 00:01:42.399
Well, her name is Lindsay and
she seems to really love you

00:01:42.399 --> 00:01:45.044
because she does put up with
I hear a lot of recordings

00:01:45.044 --> 00:01:46.265
that you do.
- Yes.

00:01:46.265 --> 00:01:49.438
- So you make the
recordings in bed, right?

00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:50.271
- Well that's one of the--

00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:52.571
- Not that kind of recording
you dirty, dirty people.

00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:53.738
- Edit that out.

00:01:53.738 --> 00:01:55.760
Yeah, that's one of
the things I do to her.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.231
I like when, once she's asleep I will have

00:01:58.231 --> 00:02:00.169
preset things on my nightstand,

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:01.002
on my side of the bed.

00:02:01.002 --> 00:02:01.977
- I love how thought out you are.

00:02:01.977 --> 00:02:03.778
- Oh, I spend a substantial amount of time

00:02:03.778 --> 00:02:06.373
thinking about how to mess with
other people in this world.

00:02:06.373 --> 00:02:08.081
(Kelly Laughs)

00:02:08.081 --> 00:02:09.114
- You better not become friends with me,

00:02:09.114 --> 00:02:10.031
like you're friends with me--
- Beware

00:02:10.031 --> 00:02:11.899
- Because it'll be coming your way.

00:02:11.899 --> 00:02:12.795
- I love it.

00:02:12.795 --> 00:02:15.448
- So anyway, I think of things
to set on the nightstand

00:02:15.448 --> 00:02:18.280
that, you know, might sound good.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.587
- I think we have an example.

00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:23.039
So here's an example of
how you mess with her.

00:02:23.039 --> 00:02:26.407
(crunching sound)

00:02:26.407 --> 00:02:28.111
- [Lindsay] What you doing?

00:02:28.111 --> 00:02:30.141
- [Eric] Having some Corn Nuts.

00:02:30.141 --> 00:02:31.912
(crunching sound)

00:02:31.912 --> 00:02:35.312
- [Lindsay] You're having
Corn Nuts right now?

00:02:35.312 --> 00:02:36.523
- [Eric] It's like puffed up corn.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.252
(crunching sound)

00:02:39.252 --> 00:02:40.390
- [Lindsay] Wait, am I gonna
have to come over there

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.557
and take them?

00:02:42.803 --> 00:02:44.467
- [Eric] You better not.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.620
- [Lindsay] I will throw them away.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.121
- [Eric] Okay, and I will
retrieve them out of the crash.

00:02:48.121 --> 00:02:48.954
(audience laughs)

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:50.252
- [Lindsay] Oh gosh.

00:02:50.252 --> 00:02:52.790
- [Eric] Mmm! I haven't
Corn Nuts in forever!

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.849
- [Lindsay] Could you
do it in the daytime?

00:02:54.849 --> 00:02:57.186
- Could you do it in the daytime?

00:02:57.186 --> 00:02:58.811
(audience applauds)

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.803
I love that she sounds like
such a mom when she was like,

00:03:01.803 --> 00:03:04.762
"Do you think that's an
appropriate snack to have in bed?"

00:03:04.762 --> 00:03:06.243
- Oh, no.

00:03:06.243 --> 00:03:07.876
But it all started with walkie talkies

00:03:07.876 --> 00:03:09.848
because I have walkie
talkies with her boys

00:03:09.848 --> 00:03:10.939
that we mess around with.

00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:11.772
- I love that.

00:03:11.772 --> 00:03:14.580
- So I quietly set one
up on her side of the bed

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.808
and turned it on.

00:03:15.808 --> 00:03:17.313
And then after she'd gone to sleep,

00:03:17.313 --> 00:03:19.246
I'm like, Lindsay, can come here?

00:03:19.246 --> 00:03:20.079
(both laugh)

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:21.179
- Oh my God.

00:03:21.179 --> 00:03:22.084
- That's where it started.

00:03:22.084 --> 00:03:23.689
- Does she ever lose it on you?

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:25.054
- She does lose it on me.

00:03:25.054 --> 00:03:26.463
I think probably one--

00:03:26.463 --> 00:03:27.296
- Do you enjoy that?

00:03:27.296 --> 00:03:28.689
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:30.228
- Yes I do, but I remind her;

00:03:30.228 --> 00:03:32.244
It's like, think of all the boring people

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:33.077
you could be with in this life--

00:03:33.077 --> 00:03:34.091
- Exactly.
- Right.

00:03:34.091 --> 00:03:35.005
- I'm exciting--

00:03:35.005 --> 00:03:36.002
- And I'm exciting.

00:03:36.002 --> 00:03:37.420
You'd never know what's coming.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.004
But I think probably one of
the most frequent sentences

00:03:41.004 --> 00:03:42.369
screamed in our house is

00:03:42.369 --> 00:03:45.461
"Eric you are 50 years old."

00:03:45.461 --> 00:03:47.495
Like you are 50.

00:03:47.495 --> 00:03:48.405
- But a child at heart.

00:03:48.405 --> 00:03:49.368
- Yes.
- Yes, exactly.

00:03:49.368 --> 00:03:50.665
- I'll never let that go.

00:03:50.665 --> 00:03:52.047
- I don't think, don't let that dream die.

00:03:52.047 --> 00:03:52.880
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.927
- Well, speaking of birthdays,
is it true that you performed

00:03:54.927 --> 00:03:56.663
at birthday parties is a
clown when you were a kid?

00:03:56.663 --> 00:03:57.496
- Oh yes.

00:03:57.496 --> 00:03:58.329
- I love this.

00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:00.173
And actually I can see that at happening.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.774
- Yeah, I mean, I have
been a clown I think,

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:03.607
oh, there I am.

00:04:03.607 --> 00:04:05.948
- This is awesome.
- Yeah.

00:04:05.948 --> 00:04:07.648
- It's a line in one of the
episodes of "Modern Family."

00:04:07.648 --> 00:04:09.769
Once I found out that "Modern Family"

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:12.906
or clowns were just
regular people with makeup

00:04:12.906 --> 00:04:15.899
I was like, well, that's what
I want to do with my life.

00:04:15.899 --> 00:04:19.193
And so my grandma started
making me clown costumes

00:04:19.193 --> 00:04:23.067
and I started putting on my mom's makeup.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.147
- She loved that.

00:04:24.147 --> 00:04:26.931
- But this is where I
always say I'm so thankful

00:04:26.931 --> 00:04:28.553
for the great parents that I had,

00:04:28.553 --> 00:04:32.333
that my dad being a Kansas
man and me a Kansas boy

00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:35.750
here I am playing football, raising pigs,

00:04:36.646 --> 00:04:38.121
taking karate, playing the drums

00:04:38.121 --> 00:04:40.100
and putting on my mom's makeup

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:40.933
and wanting to put on a wig.

00:04:40.933 --> 00:04:41.801
And he was just like--

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.134
- Yep.
- Go for it--

00:04:43.134 --> 00:04:43.967
(audience laughs)

00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:44.800
You Know?
- Love it.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:45.739
- And it 100%--

00:04:45.739 --> 00:04:46.681
- That's a real dad, that's a great dad--

00:04:46.681 --> 00:04:47.820
- Led me to right here.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.653
(audience applaud)

00:04:48.653 --> 00:04:49.683
- Yeah, I love that though.

00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:52.505
I think clowns is something,
you love to make people laugh.

00:04:52.505 --> 00:04:53.527
You love to make people feel good.

00:04:53.527 --> 00:04:54.624
- To bring joy to people's lives.

00:04:54.624 --> 00:04:55.954
- Exactly--
- And I get--

00:04:55.954 --> 00:04:57.898
- You're making a joke,
but you truly love that--

00:04:57.898 --> 00:04:59.356
- A hundred percent.
- Yeah.

00:04:59.356 --> 00:05:00.345
- That's what I tell Lindsay all the time.

00:05:00.345 --> 00:05:01.494
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:01.494 --> 00:05:02.327
- When she yells at me--

00:05:02.327 --> 00:05:03.160
- I'm just bringing joy--

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:03.993
- "You're 50.

00:05:03.993 --> 00:05:05.573
"Take the Corn Nuts somewhere else."

00:05:05.573 --> 00:05:06.406
- Yeah.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:07.689
- So we were talking about
your engagement earlier, right?

00:05:07.689 --> 00:05:08.522
- Yeah.

00:05:08.522 --> 00:05:10.708
- So how did your "Modern
Family" co-star kind of react

00:05:10.708 --> 00:05:12.025
cause you're on a show that long

00:05:12.025 --> 00:05:13.331
you built such relationships
with these people.

00:05:13.331 --> 00:05:14.354
- Yeah, there they are.

00:05:14.354 --> 00:05:16.314
- Were they like freaking out for you?

00:05:16.314 --> 00:05:18.462
(audience applauds)

00:05:18.462 --> 00:05:19.892
- Well, they were very happy

00:05:19.892 --> 00:05:21.594
when Lindsay and I started dating.

00:05:21.594 --> 00:05:24.330
I think, I was the kind
of the last holdout

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.555
everybody else had...

00:05:25.555 --> 00:05:27.311
The adults had partners.

00:05:27.311 --> 00:05:28.144
And when I met Lindsay--

00:05:28.144 --> 00:05:29.047
- They were adulting?

00:05:29.047 --> 00:05:29.880
- Yeah.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.495
- And when I met Lindsay and
started bringing her around

00:05:32.495 --> 00:05:34.626
everyone was just in love with
her right from the get go.

00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:37.177
So, when I asked her to marry
me, they were very excited.

00:05:37.177 --> 00:05:39.194
And of course, Julie,
once when we were out here

00:05:39.194 --> 00:05:41.159
she's like, I'm coming
over to see the ring.

00:05:41.159 --> 00:05:42.893
And she was very interesting--

00:05:42.893 --> 00:05:43.726
- How about that she said the ring.

00:05:43.726 --> 00:05:44.584
- Oh God, yes.

00:05:44.584 --> 00:05:45.417
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:46.921
She's like, that's what she
needed to see right after that.

00:05:46.921 --> 00:05:47.754
- I love it.

00:05:47.754 --> 00:05:48.957
- It passed her inspection,

00:05:48.957 --> 00:05:50.843
which if it passes Julie's inspection

00:05:50.843 --> 00:05:51.676
and Sophia's inspection--

00:05:51.676 --> 00:05:53.342
- You've nailed it.
- You're good.

00:05:53.342 --> 00:05:54.175
- I love that.

00:05:54.175 --> 00:05:55.008
It's always good.

00:05:55.008 --> 00:05:56.102
I feel like to have your
friends' approval of people

00:05:56.102 --> 00:05:57.046
they can, you know?

00:05:57.046 --> 00:05:57.879
- Yeah.

00:05:57.879 --> 00:05:58.809
- Sometimes you have blinders on,

00:05:58.809 --> 00:05:59.876
but they'll point it out, that's awesome.

00:05:59.876 --> 00:06:01.165
They'll love her right after that that's--

00:06:01.165 --> 00:06:01.998
- Yeah, they loved her.

00:06:01.998 --> 00:06:03.864
- So wait, so did you move back to Kansas

00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:04.697
since "Modern Family" ended?

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.797
- Back and forth, but you know, that's--

00:06:06.797 --> 00:06:07.630
- Do you like going home?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.463
Is it kinda--

00:06:08.463 --> 00:06:10.916
- I love being home and you
know, not to bring it down.

00:06:10.916 --> 00:06:12.922
I lost my dad in November and being there

00:06:12.922 --> 00:06:15.931
the last year and a half
back and forth with him

00:06:15.931 --> 00:06:18.036
was just like bonus found time

00:06:18.036 --> 00:06:19.560
that I never in a million years

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.879
thought I would end up having.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:22.477
So while the pandemic's been terrible

00:06:22.477 --> 00:06:24.031
for a lot of people and awful,

00:06:24.031 --> 00:06:26.789
it was good that I got to
spend so much quality time

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:27.652
with my dad before we lost him.

00:06:27.652 --> 00:06:29.472
- 100%, and you got that time in.

00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:30.680
- Yep.
- Wow.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.357
Well, you mentioned that
you grew up farming pigs.

00:06:33.357 --> 00:06:34.190
- Mm-hmm.
- That's amazing.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.694
- Yep, because of my dad.

00:06:36.694 --> 00:06:38.378
- I love that though was that fun?

00:06:38.378 --> 00:06:40.226
- Well, my friends got jobs, you know,

00:06:40.226 --> 00:06:42.074
like little little kid jobs

00:06:42.074 --> 00:06:43.616
like delivering papers
or helping their dads--

00:06:43.616 --> 00:06:44.449
- Yeah, mowing the lawn--

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:45.282
- Right.

00:06:45.282 --> 00:06:46.185
And so I said, "Well, I wanna get a job."

00:06:46.185 --> 00:06:47.574
And he said, "You don't need a job."

00:06:47.574 --> 00:06:48.985
And I said, "Well, I want to get a job."

00:06:48.985 --> 00:06:49.818
And he said, "All right."

00:06:49.818 --> 00:06:51.494
So one Saturday we drove to Nebraska

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:53.245
and got 60 pigs and built fence.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:54.675
And from the fourth grade on

00:06:54.675 --> 00:06:56.773
I was raising pigs in my backyard.

00:06:56.773 --> 00:06:57.853
- That's awesome.
- Yeah.

00:06:57.853 --> 00:06:58.811
- I love animals so much.

00:06:58.811 --> 00:06:59.644
I love farms--

00:06:59.644 --> 00:07:00.577
- But pigs are the best.

00:07:00.577 --> 00:07:01.871
- And growing up on them
though, you can tell too

00:07:01.871 --> 00:07:04.335
your personality is such a type that like

00:07:04.335 --> 00:07:06.255
you can tell you grew up
in some kind of environment

00:07:06.255 --> 00:07:07.179
where everybody pitched in.

00:07:07.179 --> 00:07:08.012
- Yeah.

00:07:08.012 --> 00:07:08.845
- Like you're one of those people--

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:11.277
- Well, what, having animals
to that level teaches you

00:07:11.277 --> 00:07:14.342
is that the world exists outside
your three foot perimeter.

00:07:14.342 --> 00:07:15.575
Right?
- Your egocentric zone, yeah.

00:07:15.575 --> 00:07:17.958
- Yeah, if I don't feed
my animals after school

00:07:17.958 --> 00:07:20.955
and before I go to school,
they don't sustain life.

00:07:20.955 --> 00:07:22.294
It's up to me to do that.

00:07:22.294 --> 00:07:24.549
So it's good having
something that relies on you

00:07:24.549 --> 00:07:25.445
at a young age.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:26.957
- I think my plants are
speaking to me right now.

00:07:26.957 --> 00:07:27.790
(all laugh)

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.178
- Orchids like, "Yeah, can
you talk to Kelly about that?"

00:07:30.178 --> 00:07:31.528
- "Water would be great."

00:07:31.528 --> 00:07:34.216
I'm like, it rained the other
day and it never rains here.

00:07:34.216 --> 00:07:35.379
And I was like, God bless.

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:36.647
It's just I didn't have
time and I was like--

00:07:36.647 --> 00:07:37.764
- Kelly, I got news for you,

00:07:37.764 --> 00:07:38.597
It doesn't rain inside.

00:07:38.597 --> 00:07:40.577
- No, they're outside.
- Oh okay.

00:07:40.577 --> 00:07:41.410
- They're outside.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.170
I get the ones inside, but sometimes

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.481
it's like you're a single parent,

00:07:44.481 --> 00:07:45.314
you're putting them to bed.

00:07:45.314 --> 00:07:47.033
You're doing all the things,
you're prepping for show.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:47.866
it's you forget?

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:48.736
- Yeah, so people--

00:07:48.736 --> 00:07:49.933
- And I walked outside
and one of my flowers

00:07:49.933 --> 00:07:52.005
literally just looks sad and bend over--

00:07:52.005 --> 00:07:53.618
- But then how great is it,
when they're like back up

00:07:53.618 --> 00:07:54.451
and you're like, you're welcome.

00:07:54.451 --> 00:07:55.916
- Exactly.
(audience laughs)

00:07:55.916 --> 00:07:57.740
Oh, I see you're a glass half full.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:58.791
I like it--

00:07:58.791 --> 00:08:01.117
- This is fun and this is
what makes a good TV show.

00:08:01.117 --> 00:08:02.564
We're just talking right now.

00:08:02.564 --> 00:08:04.228
- That's my goal.

00:08:04.228 --> 00:08:05.808
Thank you, that's my goal
to make it conversational.

00:08:05.808 --> 00:08:07.370
(audience applauds)

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.921
I do wanna talk about, cause
we were talking about your show

00:08:09.921 --> 00:08:10.754
while we were watching it.

00:08:10.754 --> 00:08:11.587
- Yeah.

00:08:11.587 --> 00:08:14.924
- I'm actually obsessed with
like watching domino's fall

00:08:14.924 --> 00:08:18.203
is so somehow therapeutic
and like, I love it.

00:08:18.203 --> 00:08:19.855
It's like how people like ASMR.

00:08:19.855 --> 00:08:20.740
Like I love watching that sound--

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.155
- Well there's that in there too.

00:08:22.155 --> 00:08:24.459
The sound is so good.
- The sound is awesome.

00:08:24.459 --> 00:08:25.293
- So it's intense.

00:08:25.293 --> 00:08:26.928
I will tell you, this is
what I tell everybody.

00:08:26.928 --> 00:08:29.397
This show is like camping, it's intense.

00:08:29.397 --> 00:08:30.783
(all laughs)

00:08:30.783 --> 00:08:33.888
- Dad jokes?
- Dad jokes, hello?

00:08:33.888 --> 00:08:34.721
- I love it.

00:08:34.721 --> 00:08:37.090
- The dads are laughing,
look at these guys over here.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.083
This guy is great!

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.690
(Erick imitates belly laughter)

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.805
- Wait, but it's it's
Domino Masters, right?

00:08:42.805 --> 00:08:44.053
- Yeah, Domino Masters
is the name of the show,

00:08:44.053 --> 00:08:44.934
March 9th.

00:08:44.934 --> 00:08:48.855
It's incredible, I mean,
what I loved about it

00:08:48.855 --> 00:08:49.880
is exactly what you said,

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.616
which is, I've watched
these YouTube videos

00:08:51.616 --> 00:08:53.701
of people setting up
root Goldberg machines,

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:55.154
chain reactions, dominoes

00:08:55.154 --> 00:08:56.602
in your backyard with hot wheels

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:58.241
going through the yards
and all that stuff.

00:08:58.241 --> 00:08:59.365
I was always obsessed with that.

00:08:59.365 --> 00:09:02.037
So when this show kind of came in my world

00:09:02.037 --> 00:09:03.804
I asked the nine year old
boys who live in my house,

00:09:03.804 --> 00:09:05.895
Lindsay's boys, like, have
you heard of this stuff?

00:09:05.895 --> 00:09:06.728
And they're like,

00:09:06.728 --> 00:09:08.798
" Oh, we watch domino
videos all the time."

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:10.021
And I was like, all right,
well, let's have that meeting,

00:09:10.021 --> 00:09:11.350
let's hear about it.
- Yeah.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.267
- And they sold me on it.

00:09:12.267 --> 00:09:15.067
And I just love celebrating these people

00:09:15.067 --> 00:09:17.486
who have dedicated their
lives to setting up dominoes.

00:09:17.486 --> 00:09:20.530
And it's enough now for them
that a network is giving them

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.424
a TV show and honoring them.

00:09:22.424 --> 00:09:23.292
And I wanted to be part of that.

00:09:23.292 --> 00:09:24.542
- I think that that's super cool too.

00:09:24.542 --> 00:09:27.312
And also this is like, look,
this is the jerk in me.

00:09:27.312 --> 00:09:29.959
Okay, when you're on
set, has it ever happened

00:09:29.959 --> 00:09:32.998
where one has accidentally
gone off and you're like,

00:09:32.998 --> 00:09:33.849
oh my God.

00:09:33.849 --> 00:09:35.576
Because I just feel like I would cry.

00:09:35.576 --> 00:09:36.409
- Well--

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:38.593
- Putting all that up and
like, it's about to go.

00:09:38.593 --> 00:09:41.167
And like some camera
guy backs up too much.

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:43.257
- They're all very, very
careful about that stuff--

00:09:43.257 --> 00:09:44.323
- So it didn't happen?

00:09:44.323 --> 00:09:46.593
- Well, not a camera person
did knock anything over

00:09:46.593 --> 00:09:49.322
but they themselves
knock things over and--

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:51.375
- Did they weep?
- Cry.

00:09:51.375 --> 00:09:52.208
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:52.208 --> 00:09:54.376
Like when I tell you this show is intense

00:09:54.376 --> 00:09:57.190
you have everything, you
have the drama of it,

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.419
the emotion of it because it's 16 hours,

00:09:59.419 --> 00:10:02.484
they're working on this
400 square foot area,

00:10:02.484 --> 00:10:04.317
full of dominoes.

00:10:04.317 --> 00:10:06.202
There are fields, they
call 'em domino fields.

00:10:06.202 --> 00:10:07.141
I learned all the terminology.

00:10:07.141 --> 00:10:08.432
But anyway--
- I'm so hip.

00:10:08.432 --> 00:10:10.669
- Yeah, I'm really down
with the domino people.

00:10:10.669 --> 00:10:15.669
But anyway, there's fields of
5,000 dominoes in one square.

00:10:16.183 --> 00:10:18.275
That they took for six hours to set up.

00:10:18.275 --> 00:10:19.135
- Oh my God--

00:10:19.135 --> 00:10:21.248
- There's a million dominoes on the show

00:10:21.248 --> 00:10:22.510
that they have at their disposal

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.663
of every color and
everything you can imagine.

00:10:24.663 --> 00:10:26.624
- I'm totally gonna watch, I'm so excited.

00:10:26.624 --> 00:10:29.306
- Yeah it's great, you're gonna love it.

00:10:29.306 --> 00:10:30.537
You'll all love it.

00:10:30.537 --> 00:10:31.973
- You specifically.

00:10:31.973 --> 00:10:33.092
(Kelly laughs)

